1
00:00:02,500 --> 00:00:04,492
Every school should observe lessons.

2
00:00:04,492 --> 00:00:07,280
Very few can show what happens next.

3
00:00:07,280 --> 00:00:18,036
This is the Observation System: one route from lesson observation, to collected evidence, to a coaching plan for every teacher, covering every step of the learning journey.

4
00:00:18,036 --> 00:00:20,028
Here is the whole journey.

5
00:00:22,028 --> 00:00:23,813
It starts in the classroom.

6
00:00:23,813 --> 00:00:38,089
The teacher coach opens one form and fills in the observation details: subject, class and teacher, with live dropdowns fed by the school's own staff directory, so nothing is typed from memory and no list is ever out of date.

7
00:00:38,089 --> 00:00:40,230
Class composition is a few taps.

8
00:00:40,230 --> 00:00:43,799
The whole context of the lesson, captured throughout the observation.

9
00:00:44,249 --> 00:00:52,822
Each observation uses the Regulatory Body's own six point scale, from Very Weak to Outstanding, with the same proportion bands its inspectors already use.

10
00:00:52,822 --> 00:00:58,538
Ten criteria, from attainment and progress to teaching and leadership, each with room for a comment.

11
00:00:58,538 --> 00:01:04,968
The form speaks the language of inspection, because it was built to coach teachers using the same criteria.

12
00:01:05,418 --> 00:01:07,220
Coaching notes can be handwritten.

13
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:10,825
The form has an Evidence Pad, designed for Apple Pencil.

14
00:01:10,825 --> 00:01:17,674
The observer types, or writes with the Pencil, and keeps photos of the board or the pupils' work alongside.

15
00:01:17,674 --> 00:01:21,279
The system reads the handwriting and turns it into text.

16
00:01:21,279 --> 00:01:26,326
Everything is saved automatically throughout the observation, so nothing is ever lost mid lesson.

17
00:01:26,776 --> 00:01:33,319
When it is done, each observation gets its own ID, freezes, and everything is saved, ready for review.

18
00:01:33,768 --> 00:01:36,626
One tap files everything, four ways at once.

19
00:01:36,626 --> 00:01:38,769
The observation lands in a spreadsheet.

20
00:01:38,769 --> 00:01:42,341
It mirrors into a live database, duplicate proof by design.

21
00:01:42,341 --> 00:01:49,842
A branded backup email goes to the observer, for safe keeping and easy access, with a link to the locked observation.

22
00:01:49,842 --> 00:01:55,915
And the handwriting itself is archived in private storage, so it can be reviewed if ever needed.

23
00:01:58,916 --> 00:02:01,399
Now the other end of the pipeline.

24
00:02:01,399 --> 00:02:05,300
The Observation Dashboard opens with a password, safety as a priority.

25
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:08,492
As an example, here is one school's June round.

26
00:02:08,492 --> 00:02:15,586
The story plays itself: a hundred and eleven lessons, a hundred and five teachers, counted up live from the data.

27
00:02:15,586 --> 00:02:18,423
Where judgements sit on the six point scale.

28
00:02:18,423 --> 00:02:19,487
What is working.

29
00:02:19,487 --> 00:02:20,906
Where to focus next.

30
00:02:20,906 --> 00:02:27,999
And one tap presents that round's findings in full screen, built to showcase the round by itself in any meeting.

31
00:02:28,449 --> 00:02:34,351
Every written statement carries a small number: a citation, a reference stemming from an actual observation.

32
00:02:34,351 --> 00:02:42,835
Click or tap to open the references and see the actual observations behind each statement: subject, date, judgement, and the inspector's words, verbatim.

33
00:02:42,835 --> 00:02:47,261
AI cites the hundreds of references that sit behind every claimed statement.

34
00:02:47,261 --> 00:02:50,581
Nothing on this dashboard is an opinion without evidence.

35
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:53,537
Rounds can be compared to show movement.

36
00:02:53,537 --> 00:03:02,489
Every teacher seen in both rounds is displayed as a line, from where they were to where they are, green when they moved toward Outstanding.

37
00:03:02,489 --> 00:03:06,427
A transition matrix counts the improvements, the holds and the declines.

38
00:03:06,427 --> 00:03:10,366
This is the question governors actually ask: is teaching getting better?

39
00:03:10,366 --> 00:03:11,441
If not, why?

40
00:03:11,441 --> 00:03:13,231
And how can we improve?

41
00:03:13,682 --> 00:03:18,465
The Dashboard shows Coverage, which answers the other question: who has been seen?

42
00:03:18,465 --> 00:03:26,560
Teachers on the register, teachers observed, lessons per teacher, and who is still waiting, so no one is invisible for a term.

43
00:03:29,059 --> 00:03:32,058
Drill into any teacher and their history follows.

44
00:03:32,058 --> 00:03:35,806
Two gauges, student progress and teaching, averaged across every observation.

45
00:03:35,806 --> 00:03:39,554
Each session, its skills and its notes, one card each.

46
00:03:39,554 --> 00:03:55,671
And below them, a coaching plan: drafted by AI from that teacher's own lessons, checked word for word against the source, grounded in the school's own rubric, then amended if needed and approved by the teacher coach before the teacher ever sees it.

47
00:03:56,121 --> 00:03:57,924
Teachers have their own door.

48
00:03:57,924 --> 00:04:05,494
A portal for every member of staff: their photograph, their history, and a notification when a new coaching plan is approved.

49
00:04:05,494 --> 00:04:09,100
What they see is deliberately thinner than what leadership sees.

50
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:16,310
No observer's rough notes, no edits, no other teachers, only their own approved coaching plan and their own next steps.

51
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:28,578
For the leadership table, one button turns the round into a governance report, simple or in depth, and a second builds it as a branded Google Doc, all references attached, teachers anonymised by construction.

52
00:04:28,578 --> 00:04:37,963
When a new round lands, one more button rewrites the analysis for it, the AI's work double checked by the Head of Teaching and Learning before publishing.

53
00:04:38,413 --> 00:04:39,532
Underneath, three locks.

54
00:04:39,532 --> 00:04:41,396
A password for the school.

55
00:04:41,396 --> 00:04:44,006
A second, server verified password for administrators.

56
00:04:44,006 --> 00:04:46,989
And a unique key for every single entry.

57
00:04:46,989 --> 00:04:54,074
The whole system runs on the tools a school already pays for: Google Workspace, a database, and static hosting.

58
00:04:54,074 --> 00:05:00,413
No servers to maintain, no per seat licences, and the data stays in accounts the school controls.

59
00:05:02,913 --> 00:05:07,692
From a lesson observed, to evidence, to a plan in the teacher's hand.

60
00:05:07,692 --> 00:05:11,001
One system, built inside a school, ready to travel.

61
00:05:11,001 --> 00:05:12,104
Better never stops.
